Cell["\<\
Each operation is written as {label,R,t,flag}. Only its point action enters \
the local orbital matrix; the translation is retained so the same operation \
data can be used by init.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"2fff69db-dd56-4d20-87cf-f98834df918b"],

Cell["\<\
basis may contain scalar orbitals such as px and py or two-component spinors. \
The matrices are returned in the same operation order and act on the basis in \
the order supplied.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"05846039-9a8e-4c0e-b1f2-6f57df2163a3"],

Cell["\<\
For an ordered basis {f1,...,fn}, column j contains the coefficients of the \
transformed state g fj in that same basis: g fj = Sum_i fi D_ij(g).\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4b3857f0-e07b-44f7-9458-1667bd061f03"]
}, Closed]],

